  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "xmlrpc-c security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for xmlrpc-c is now available for openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "XML-RPC is a quick-and-easy way to make procedure calls  over the Internet. It converts the procedure call into  an XML document, sends it to a remote server using HTTP,  and gets back the response as XML.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nXMLRPC-C Library versions 1.07 through 1.67.01 are vulnerable to a reflected cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in the error page component.(CVE-2026-15928)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for xmlrpc-c is now available for openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "xmlrpc-c",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
